CORE no-new-smt
main.c
--floatbv
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Round-to-integral (rintf, rint, __CPROVER_round_to_integralf) under all rounding
modes, for special values, subnormals, ties, already-integral values, and
formats with 4-, 2- and 1-bit exponents, including rounding up to infinity.
The inputs are nondeterministic, so that the flattening encoding is used rather
than constant folding.
